{
 "_schema": "groot-virtual-robot-bench/sonic-latefix/1",
 "date": "2026-10-14",
 "tag": "MEASURED",
 "tag_note": "counts and timings MEASURED, rebuilt by sonic/make_sonic_table.py from results/sonic/raw/ (groups <board>/fix_*, <board>/stock_sameday_unloaded and the first-campaign groups); scheduling readbacks and GR00T rates are a published record (MEASURED, raw not published); sums and slowdowns DERIVED",
 "what": "A deployment change to NVIDIA's GEAR-SONIC deploy on the Jetson AGX Orin 64 GB and the Jetson AGX Thor: the control thread runs at SCHED_FIFO 90 and the main loop sleeps, instead of upstream's busy-spinning FIFO-99 main thread. The first campaign's unloaded, CPU-saturated and GPU co-tenant arms were repeated with it (3 runs each) and compared with the stock runs.",
 "change": {
  "summary": "control thread SCHED_FIFO 90 + sleeping main loop instead of upstream's busy-spinning FIFO-99 main thread",
  "detail": "(1) the control thread sets SCHED_FIFO at the priority in SONIC_CTRL_FIFO on itself at its first Control() call; (2) with SONIC_MAIN_SLEEP=abs, upstream main()'s sleep(0.02) (an unsigned sleep(), so sleep(0): a spin of the SCHED_FIFO-99, CPU0-pinned main thread when run as root) is replaced by clock_nanosleep(CLOCK_MONOTONIC, TIMER_ABSTIME) on a 20 ms grid. Both are inert when the variables are unset. Patch: sonic/harness/latefix.patch (applies on top of sonic_probe.patch).",
  "env": "SONIC_CTRL_FIFO=90, SONIC_MAIN_SLEEP=abs",
  "privileges": "needs root or CAP_SYS_NICE (SCHED_FIFO); the Jetson runs ran as root, as in the first campaign",
  "clocks": "unchanged: nvpmodel MAXN + jetson_clocks on both Jetsons, read back in every run",
  "binaries_sha256": {
   "orin_fix": "cdd1e4b3384e0e7db236a37366753d7f4f98d8cddc18c8461bad724ff0719329",
   "thor_fix": "827a13f22e290f9c9b8d15b0e2c7921eddf04770c9230c622fbf10ad70a0435f",
   "orin_stock": "082aaa6a425daf0c327939613669808c3e8924449002cee9af7a9f41b88c86f3",
   "thor_stock": "b8558951dcff0c5b99c525afa77399ffacac203e7d25718523cc8b1baa344caf"
  },
  "not_applicable": "the deploy constructs no onnxruntime session on the Jetsons (planner, encoder and decoder are TensorRT engines), so there is no CPU inference thread pool to restrict"
 },
 "versions": "as in results/sonic/sonic_thor_2026-10-14.json and sonic_orin_2026-10-14.json (same board software, engines, simulator)",
 "clocks": {
  "orin": "PINNED: nvpmodel MAXN + jetson_clocks (run again at session start; read back identical to the pre-existing lock): CPU 12x min=max=cur 2201600 kHz (governor schedutil, floored), GPU min=max=cur 1300.5 MHz, EMC 3199 MHz FreqOverride=1. Read back while stress-ng ran: all 12 cores at 2201600 kHz.",
  "thor": "PINNED: nvpmodel MAXN + jetson_clocks (run again at session start; read back identical to the pre-existing lock): CPU 14x governor performance min=max=cur 2601000 kHz, gpu-gpc-0 min=max=cur 1575 MHz, gpu-nvd-0 1692 MHz, EMC min=max=cur 4266 MHz."
 },
 "design": "per board, in this order, 15 s apart: one same-session stock unloaded run (stockref_cl_r1, the readback reference), then with the fix: unloaded x3 (fix_cl_r1-3), CPU saturated x3 (fix_a4cpu_r1-3: stress-ng --cpu $(nproc) --cpu-method matrixprod), GPU co-tenant x3 (fix_a4gpu_r1-3: GR00T N1.5 full TensorRT back-to-back on the same GPU, 60 s alone first). Stock rows are the first campaign's runs from earlier the same day (same binaries, engines, clocks, script, harness; not interleaved). Batch: sonic/harness/jetson_runs.sh fix <orin|thor>.",
 "preregistration": "predictions written before the first measured run of the fix (after one 8 s function-only smoke run per board whose run dir was deleted)",
