 "findings": [
  "CPU saturated, AGX Orin: 571 compute misses / 567 slot misses / 686 late starts (stock, 3 runs) -> 0 / 0 / 0 with the fix (max start-to-start gap 20.20 ms, step max 8.85 ms). MEASURED.",
  "CPU saturated, AGX Thor: 11 compute / 16 slot / 316 late starts (stock) -> 0 / 0 / 0 (max gap 20.02 ms). The first campaign's non-root diagnostic (no FIFO-99 spin, control thread SCHED_OTHER) still had 8 slot misses and 273 late starts on Thor, so the busy-spin was not the whole story there: the rest fits the control thread queuing behind the CPU hogs, which FIFO 90 removes. MEASURED; the mechanism is INFERRED (no scheduler trace).",
  "Unloaded: 0 compute / 0 slot misses on both boards with the fix, as stock. MEASURED.",
  "GPU co-tenant (GR00T N1.5 full TensorRT), AGX Orin: compute misses 91 -> 46 (per run 30/31/30 -> 14/16/16), late starts 82 -> 44, but slot misses 6 -> 10 (n = 3 each, not interleaved). The remaining > 20 ms steps are attributed to GPU time shared with GR00T, which a CPU priority cannot fix (INFERRED, not traced). Thor: 0 compute / 0 slot misses with or without the fix; late starts 6 -> 0. GR00T itself slowed less beside the fixed controller (Orin 9.5% vs 13.4%; Thor 5.8% vs 6.5%), output unchanged. MEASURED (slowdown DERIVED).",
  "Falls (D1 rule): with the fix Orin 3/9 (unloaded 1/3, CPU 1/3, GPU 1/3; each went down 0.5-0.7 s after the band-off command), Thor 0/9. The fix removes the Orin CPU-arm collapse (stock 3/3, falling throughout the run) but not the band-drop falls, which occur with clean timing on both binaries (see the controlled band-drop test). With the fix, Orin tracking failed in 1 of 3 CPU-saturated runs (the run that fell). MEASURED.",
  "Variable moved: the control thread was SCHED_FIFO 90 at all three readbacks in 18/18 fix runs (stock: SCHED_OTHER); main-thread CPU over the control window 25.02% -> <= 0.03% of a core on Orin and 13.68% -> <= 0.02% on Thor. MEASURED.",
  "Simulator starvation, reported separately (the hogs also starve the Python simulator on the same CPU): Thor sim overrun steps 332/205/379 (stock) -> 248/105/139 (fix); Orin 297/36/92 -> 2/8/0. The Orin drop was not predicted and its cause is not verified. MEASURED counts."
 ],
 "caveats": [
  "sim2sim only: MuJoCo on the same board, DDS over loopback, no real G1",
  "3 runs per arm; the CPU-arm eliminations (571 -> 0, 11 -> 0) are far outside run-to-run spread; the Orin GPU-arm halving is consistent across runs but not interleaved with the stock runs (earlier the same day)",
  "the fix changes upstream's deployment and needs root or CAP_SYS_NICE on the robot computer",
  "AGX Orin 64 GB developer kit, not the G1's Orin NX (fewer cores, smaller GPU): not measured",
  "no scheduler trace on the Jetsons: mechanisms are inferred from the arms and /proc readbacks"
 ],
